  "conclusions": {
    "rootCause": "Under host pids=32 with init, failed starts coincide with pids.events max events and a measured peak of 32 host tasks. The same guest program succeeds with host pids=64/128. Sentry, gofer and systrap host processes/threads require a separate cgroup budget.",
    "errnoBoundary": "The exact source conversion that surfaces host PID exhaustion as exec ENOMEM was not traced. PID exhaustion is established by the repeated host cgroup measurements, not inferred from the ENOMEM text alone.",
    "interpreted": {
      "hostPids": 128,
      "guestNproc": 32,
      "keepInit": true,
      "evidence": "At guest nproc=32 the successful fork probes stop at 30 children with errno EAGAIN; init and the parent consume two guest tasks. Thread probes also stop at 30 guest threads. Host pids=64 fails before reaching the guest quota.",
